{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cf5mutvseJ16D2W4kvQTn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a complete understanding of the repository structure. Let me analyze the repository findings and conventions:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- **Order.kt:line 11-16**: Order data class lacks status field\n- **OrderRepository.kt:line 11-27**: In-memory store with basic CRUD, no shipment queries\n- **OrderController.kt:line 17-46**: Only create, get by ID, and list endpoints exist\n- **ShipmentRepository.kt:line 11-27**: In-memory store; needs findByOrderId method  \n- **ShipmentController.kt:line 26-44**: Create endpoint lacks order status validation\n- **ApiError.kt:line 31-37**: ErrorCode enum needs ORDER_CANCELLED code\n- **ApiExceptions.kt, GlobalExceptionHandler.kt**: Exception infrastructure ready\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- HTTP 201 CREATED for successful POST, 200 OK for GET\n- HTTP 404 NOT_FOUND for missing resources, 409 CONFLICT for state violations\n- Centralized error envelope via GlobalExceptionHandler: `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [...]}}`\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException, ConflictException) with ErrorCode and message\n- Repositories are autowired into controllers\n- Tests verify both status code and error envelope structure\n\n**Affected files - must change:**\n1. **Order.kt** - Add status field and OrderStatus enum\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with all validation\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add findByOrderId method for cascade cancellation\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code for shipment rejection\n\n**Risks:**\n- **Transaction atomicity**: Must check all shipments BEFORE any updates (all-or-nothing)\n- **Idempotency**: Cancelling already-cancelled order must succeed with 200 OK\n- **Integration**: OrderController needs ShipmentRepository for cascade operations\n- **State consistency**: A single CONFIRMED shipment must block the entire cancel\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirements fully specify all cases.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field (default `ACTIVE` for new orders); add enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Order>` method to support finding all shipments for an order (will use ShipmentRepository instead in controller).\n\n3. **OrderController.kt** - Inject `InMemoryShipmentRepository`; add POST endpoint `/orders/{orderId}/cancel` that:\n   - Returns 404 if order doesn't exist\n   - Returns 200 OK if order already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks if ANY shipment is CONFIRMED; if yes, throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and changes nothing\n   - If ACTIVE, sets status to CANCELLED, saves order, and cancels all CREATED shipments\n   - Returns the updated order\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to query shipments for an order.\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - Inject `InMemoryOrderRepository`; in create method, after checking for duplicate shipmentId:\n   - Check if order exists (keep current behavior for non-existent orders)\n   - Check if order status is CANCELLED; if yes, throw ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED\n   - Then proceed with shipment creation\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes.\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have used a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic, but the existing codebase has controllers calling repositories directly (no service layer), so staying consistent with that pattern is better.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Case: Cancel active order with CREATED shipments*\n- Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- OrderController retrieves order from repository (throws 404 if missing)\n- OrderController queries ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(\"O-1\")\n- OrderController checks if any shipment.status == CONFIRMED; if yes, throw ConflictException → 409\n- OrderController sets order.status = CANCELLED and saves\n- OrderController updates all CREATED shipments to CANCELLED and saves each\n- Response: 200 OK with updated order\n\n*Case: Cancel already-cancelled order*\n- Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- OrderController retrieves order (throws 404 if missing)\n- OrderController checks status == CANCELLED\n- OrderController returns 200 OK with the order unchanged (idempotent)\n\n*Case: Cancel order with CONFIRMED shipment*\n- Request: POST /orders/O-1/cancel\n- OrderController retrieves order\n- OrderController finds CONFIRMED shipment\n- OrderController throws ConflictException → 409 CONFLICT\n- Nothing changes (order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged)\n\n*Case: Create shipment for cancelled order*\n- Request: POST /shipments with orderId=\"O-1\" (already CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController checks order exists\n- ShipmentController sees order.status == CANCELLED\n- ShipmentController throws ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED → 409\n- Shipment not created\n\n*Case: Create shipment for non-existent order (unchanged behavior)*\n- Request: POST /shipments with orderId=\"MISSING\"\n- ShipmentController proceeds (existing behavior allows this)\n- Shipment created with orderId=\"MISSING\" (no validation that order exists)\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n*OrderControllerTest additions:*\n1. Test cancelling an ACTIVE order returns 200 and sets status to CANCELLED\n2. Test cancelling a CANCELLED order returns 200 (idempotent)\n3. Test cancelling order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 CONFLICT\n4. Test cancelling non-existent order returns 404 ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n5. Test cancelling order cancels all CREATED shipments\n6. Test that after cancel, order status is CANCELLED in subsequent GET\n\n*ShipmentControllerTest additions:*\n1. Test creating shipment for cancelled order returns 409 ORDER_CANCELLED\n2. Test existing shipment creation still works (ensure no regression)\n\n*OrderControllerTest regression:*\n- Verify existing tests still pass with new status field\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nLet me start implementing the design:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1284,"cache_read_input_tokens":20038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1284},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9b0e5ed8-e134-42fc-b402-d223c1ef56ae","uuid":"49bda615-b7b2-4937-a277-c87dd795f7e8","timestamp":"2026-09-15T19:27:08.269Z","request_id":"req_011Cf5mutUpoN6zsmzNkeZmQ"}
