r.kt, ShipmentController.kt, ShipmentRepository.kt, ApiError.kt\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field and `OrderStatus` enum. Necessary because orders need a lifecycle.\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Added `ShipmentRepository` injection and new `cancel` endpoint with all-or-nothing validation and cascade cancellation. Necessary to implement the cancel feature.\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId` method. Necessary for OrderController to find shipments to cancel.\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Added `OrderRepository` injection and validation to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Necessary per requirement.\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Added `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` and `ORDER_CANCELLED` error codes. Necessary for consistent error contract.\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Added comprehensive tests for cancel functionality (9 new tests). Necessary to verify implementation.\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Added tests for shipment creation with cancelled/active orders (3 new tests). Necessary to verify shipment validation.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements implemented and tested.\n\n---\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with idempotent cancellation, \n              all-or-nothing transaction semantics, and cascade cancellation of CREATED shipments\nChanged       Order.kt                    - Added status field with OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE/CANCELLED)\n              OrderController.kt          - Added /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with validation and cascade\n              ShipmentRepository.kt       - Added findByOrderId method for querying shipments by order\n              ShipmentController.kt       - Added validation to prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt                 - Added ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED and ORDER_CANCELLED error codes\n              OrderControllerTest.kt     